; for reviewers and the transformation-analyst it also denies every existing path outside the role's own areas; agent_settings.py takes the run's stage, confines each reviewer's shell to its own evidence directory docs/delivery/test-evidence/<stage>/<key> and explicitly denies the other reviewers' evidence directories even before they exist, while the transformation-analyst and implementers may write no evidence (docs/delivery/test-evidence is denied) (D-028); the only writable scratch is the run's private TMPDIR, since the sandbox allows $TMPDIR/claude-0 and leaves /tmp and /var/tmp read-only (D-028); agents start with --setting-sources project, so user or local settings cannot switch the hook off (D-025). The validator accepts a gate's review and audit records only from runs whose recorded settings (settings.json, matching meta.settings_sha256) enforce that sandbox and whose deny list names .git, .claude, tools/gates, tools/agents, docs/source, docs/delivery/reviews and docs/delivery/runs under the run's own working directory, meta.cwd (D-025, F-DG0-230). The runner's before-and-after configuration scan covers user Claude settings, git config and excludes, hooks including symlinks, and Claude configuration and ignore files anywhere in the repository and worktrees, ignored by git or not; it skips zero-length, untracked, non-symlink files (the sandbox's own stubs), reports added, changed and removed entries (a removed entry as '<path> removed', so a configuration file that is deleted or truncated to zero length, including an ignored file such as .claude/settings.local.json, is reported; snapshot entries are tab-separated so paths with spaces stay unambiguous) and fails closed (if the comparison itself fails, the run counts as changed), records changes as external_config_changed, refuses to auto-commit a reviewer or analyst run (exit 71) and warns for an implementer run (D-024, D-025, D-026, D-027)","Write guard, per-run Bash sandbox settings, scope table, validator 