-REQ-DLV-023,ENGINEERING,"Provide a gate-validation script and CI job that check schemas, reviewer identities and independence, candidate match, evidence existence, completed requirements, test outcomes and blocking findings, and exit non-zero on failure",M0067,§0.5 Evidence and mechanical enforcement,,"Stage ID;Mode (--stage, --historical, --pipeline, --register, --reconcile)","validate.mjs runs locally and in the delivery-gates CI workflow on every push and pull request; the workflow installs bubblewrap before the tests and lifts Ubuntu 24.04's AppArmor restriction on unprivileged user namespaces, because the sandbox tests treat a missing sandbox as a failure (D-026); implementers cannot edit tools/gates (write guard and Bash sandbox); before a candidate freezes, the orchestrator runs tools/gates/prefreeze.sh, which runs every check that executes candidate code through tools/gates/sandbox-run.sh: only git rev-parse runs outside, against the repository's own protected .git; the clone, the checkout and the command all run inside bubblewrap, on a tmpfs private to the sandbox's mount namespace (no other process, including another agent, can see or change the work clone), with the git directory bound read-only at /tmp/src.git, a read-only root filesystem, no network, a separate PID namespace, git hooks off and a clean environment; the clone holds only the committed HEAD, so ignored or untracked files are absent (D-026, D-027, F-DG0-141) and then proves, with trusted tools/gates code run from /, that the working-tree candidate equals HEAD (D-026); the pre-freeze also re-runs tools/source/merge_register.py in the sandboxed clone and requires docs/delivery/requirements.csv and docs/analysis/master-prompt-coverage.csv to be unchanged by it, so the register always equals the merge of the analyst part files (pre-freeze check 'register equals the merge of docs/analysis/parts (sandboxed)'; D-026)",Validator and CI job,delivery-orchestrator,"write:delivery-orchestrator(delivery